In fact, that's not entirely true.  In NH 3.1.3, wizards did not start 
out with the force bolt spell.  I ascended two wizards at the time and 
the only way to keep them alive until they had decent armor and weapons 
was to engrave Elbereth in any hallway that I passed, which was easy 
since they started out with an athame.  This kept the monsters 
distributed - they could not follow you (the rules have changed in the 
meantime, you would have to put an object on each of the Elbereth 
squares in addition...).  So it was not just a defense technique but a 
useful strategy.  And I could not have run away, because the wizards 
improved so slowly that they could not descend any further early on, and 
monsters became plentiful on any of the few levels accessible to them.
So the E-word was the right thing to do...  (and appropriate for a 
wizard anyway).
